DOC000113,04_TUG_Risk_oriented_design.docx,Mehmet/Literatur/Wordler/YTMK/2015/04_TUG_Risk_oriented_design.docx,04_TUG_Risk_oriented_design,,unknown,excavation|risk,04_TUG_Risk_oriented_design | RISK ORIENTED TUNNEL DESIGN PROCESS | INTRODUCTION | EVENTS LIKE THIS | RISK ASSESSMENT AND MANAGMENT | GENERAL PROCEDURE OF RISK EVALUATION | RISK ORIENTED DESIGN PROCESS | STRUCTURED APPROACH | GROUND BEHAVIOUR | TYPES OF FAILURE MODES | WHICH MODEL ? | EXAMPLE,"04 TUG Risk oriented design RISK ORIENTED TUNNEL DESIGN PROCESS Wulf Schubert Graz University of Technology 3G-Gruppe Geotechnik Graz ZT GmbH INTRODUCTION Accidents during tunnel construction not only have led to cost increase, time overruns, injuries and fatalities, but also contributed to a bad reputation of the industry Insurers talk of bad risk Regulations become more and more strict Lawyers and courts are increasingly involved EVENTS LIKE THIS … OR THIS … OR THIS RAISE THE QUESTIONS … Have we acted responsibly during design and construction? Have we considered the geological conditons appropriately? Are we really aware of the hazards involved? Have we used state of the art methods? RISK ASSESSMENT AND MANAGMENT Risk assessment - if conducted at all - is often understood as a separate task Underground projects are associated with uncertainties in all stages; even with perfect investigation and design, residual risks remain Thus risk assessment and management should be integrated into the whole process, from investigation through design and construction until the completion of the project GENERAL PROCEDURE OF RISK EVALUATION START Definition of the system Hazard identification R",,,excavation|risk,,2015,en,low,pending_human_review,,,
