DOC000172,Turcja_16-19_03_2015_part3.ppt,TAIEX Karayolu Tünellerinin Sınıflandırılması Eğitimi 16-19 Mart 2015/Turcja_16-19_03_2015_part3.ppt,Turcja_16-19_03_2015_part3,,unknown,,Turcja_16-19_03_2015_part3 | Slayt 1 | Slayt 2 | Slayt 3 | Slayt 4 | Slayt 5 | Slayt 6 | Slayt 7 | Slayt 8 | Slayt 9 | Slayt 10 | Slayt 11,"Turcja 16-19 03 2015 part3 Slayt 1 TAIEX Expert Mission on road tunnel categorization Katarzyna Piechowska-Strumik General Inspectorate of Road Transport in Poland Ankara, 16-19 March 2015 Slayt 2 Quantitative risk assessment model for dangerous goods transport through road tunnels QRA model Overview of the OECD/PIARC DG-QRA model The DG QRA model allows: A quantitative approach, by means of: Quantitative frequency analysis: the DG QRA model includes results of an analysis of the sequence of event from an initial event accident, breakdown accident rates on tunnel/open air routes are defined by the user, on the basis of national statistics default values, or those generally used for the tunnels project or local statistics observation of accidents for in-service roads/tunnels Quantitative conseqence analysis: a 2D and a simpler 1D tool have been implemented in the DG QRA model a separate 1D tool has been incorporated to calculate the physical and physiological consequences of scenarios in tunnels The combination of quantitative frequency and consequence analyses allows the calculation of fn curves Slayt 3 Quantitative risk assessment model for dangerous goods transport through road t",C,training_material,,,2015,tr,medium,pending_human_review,,,
DOC000173,Turcja_16-19_03_2015_part4.ppt,TAIEX Karayolu Tünellerinin Sınıflandırılması Eğitimi 16-19 Mart 2015/Turcja_16-19_03_2015_part4.ppt,Turcja_16-19_03_2015_part4,,unknown,,Turcja_16-19_03_2015_part4 | Slayt 1 | Slayt 2 | Slayt 3 | Slayt 4 | Slayt 5 | Slayt 6 | Slayt 7 | Slayt 8 | Slayt 9 | Slayt 10 | Slayt 11,"Turcja 16-19 03 2015 part4 Slayt 1 TAIEX Expert Mission on road tunnel categorization Katarzyna Piechowska-Strumik General Inspectorate of Road Transport in Poland Ankara, 16-19 March 2015 Slayt 2 Practical methods applicable for transport of dangerous goods through road tunnels AUSTRIA Austrian Road Tunnel Safety Law The Road Tunnel Safety Law translates the requirements contained in the EU Directive into Austrian law. It is applicable to all tunnels with a length exceeding 500 m of the primary road network federal roads . The road tunnel safety law defines the following measures for the transport of dangerous goods: Prior to the definition or modification of regulations and requirements regarding the transport of dangerous goods through a tunnel, a risk analysis is to be performed To enforce the regulation, appropriate signs indicating alternative routes are to be posted ahead of the last possible exit before the tunnel and at tunnel entrances Specific operating measures designed to reduce the risks related to some or all of the vehicles transporting dangerous goods in tunnels are to be checked e.g. escorted passage in convoys Slayt 3 Practical methods applicable for transport of",C,training_material,,,2015,tr,medium,pending_human_review,,,
